# XCU unalias
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# unalias is intrinsic (XCU 1.7), so it is exercised through the shell
# running the test. See alias.asr for how definitions are put to use.

assertion  XCU.unalias.001
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       unalias name removes the alias: it exits zero, alias no longer
           finds the name and the name is no longer substituted.
test       t/001-remove-one.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.002
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Every name given is removed, and an alias that was not named
           stays defined.
test       t/002-remove-several.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.003
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      1992
says       unalias -a removes all alias definitions and exits zero.
test       t/003-remove-all.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.004
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       A name that is not an alias gives an exit status greater than
           zero.
test       t/004-missing-status.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.005
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#STDERR
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.4
class      required
since      1992
says       For a name that is not an alias nothing is written to standard
           output and a diagnostic message is written to standard error.
test       t/005-missing-streams.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.006
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.13
class      required
since      1992
says       unalias run in a subshell does not remove the alias from the
           shell that started the subshell.
test       t/006-subshell.sh

assertion  XCU.unalias.007
anchor     utilities/unalias.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.4
class      required
since      1992
says       The utility accepts -- as the end of options, so unalias --
           name removes the alias.
test       t/007-double-dash.sh
